  "물이 끓다 = hervir el agua · 된장을 풀다 = disolver el doenjang.": "물이 끓다 = the water boils · 된장을 풀다 = dissolve the doenjang.",
  "Raíz verbal + -자마자 (G079) = «en cuanto». 끓다 → 끓자마자, sin marca de pasado en la primera acción.": "Verb stem + -자마자 (G079) = “as soon as”. 끓다 → 끓자마자, with no past marker on the first action.",
  "Ordena el paso que debe hacerse en cuanto hierva el agua.": "Put the step to take as soon as the water boils in order.",
  "감자 = patata · 썰다 = cortar en láminas/trozos · 물에 넣다 = poner en agua.": "감자 = potato · 썰다 = slice / cut into pieces · 물에 넣다 = put in water.",
  "썰다 → 썰자마자 (G079): la segunda acción sucede inmediatamente después de cortar.": "썰다 → 썰자마자 (G079): the second action occurs immediately after cutting.",
  "Construye la instrucción de secuencia inmediata para que la patata no se oxide.": "Build the immediate sequence instruction so that the potato does not turn brown.",
  "두부를 넣다 = añadir tofu · 불을 줄이다 = bajar el fuego.": "두부를 넣다 = add tofu · 불을 줄이다 = lower the heat.",
  "넣자마자 (G079) conecta dos acciones consecutivas sin intervalo: añadir y bajar el fuego.": "넣자마자 (G079) connects two consecutive actions without interval: add and lower the fire.",
  "Ordena la reacción inmediata que evita que el tofu se rompa.": "Put in order the immediate step that keeps the tofu from breaking apart.",
  "뚜껑 = tapa · 열다 = abrir · 파 = cebolleta.": "뚜껑 = lid · 열다 = open · 파 = scallion.",
  "열다 → 열자마자 (G079). -자마자 se une directamente a la raíz y conserva el orden inmediato.": "열다 → 열자마자 (G079). -자마자 binds directly to the root and retains the immediate order.",
  "Recupera el último gesto de la receta en cuanto se abre la tapa.": "Recover the last gesture of the recipe as soon as the lid opens.",
  "밥이 되다 = quedar listo el arroz · 뜸을 들이다 = dejar reposar al vapor.": "밥이 되다 = the rice is ready · 뜸을 들이다 = let the rice rest and steam.",
  "되다 → 되자마자 (G079), «en cuanto esté listo». 십 분 동안 indica cuánto dura el reposo posterior.": "되다 → 되자마자 (G079), \"as soon as it is ready\". 십 분 동안 indicates how long the subsequent rest will last.",
  "Ordena la instrucción para reposar el arroz en cuanto termina la cocción.": "Put in order the instruction to let the rice rest as soon as it finishes cooking.",
  "젓다 = remover · 냄새를 맡다 = oler · 할아버지는 es el sujeto de ambas acciones.": "젓다 = stir · 냄새를 맡다 = smell · 할아버지는 is the subject of both actions.",
  "-(으)면서 (G061) une dos acciones simultáneas del mismo sujeto: 저으면서 … 맡아요.": "-(으)면서 (G061) joins two simultaneous actions of the same subject: 저으면서 ... 맡아요.",
