  "El paraguas azul es falso. La humedad, sorprendentemente, no.": "The blue umbrella is fake, the humidity, surprisingly, no.",
  "La azotea bajo la lluvia (옥상 세트)": "The Rooftop in the Rain (옥상 세트)",
  "El contador sube. Ahora ya no es posible fingir que esto era un ensayo.": "Now it is no longer possible to pretend that this was a rehearsal.",
  "Episodio 16 · toma: demasiadas · resultado: todavía prometedor.": "Episode 16 · takes: too many · result: still promising.",
  "La cabina de edición (편집실)": "The Editing Booth (편집실)",
  "Las tarjetas de prensa encajan y revelan una nota al dorso: la retransmisión promocional nunca se detuvo. El público lleva viendo todo —la peluca torcida, la discusión sobre el paraguas y tu intento de esconderte detrás de una planta demasiado pequeña.\n\n서미라 observa el contador y toma una decisión peligrosamente televisiva: no ocultar el accidente, sino convertirlo en la escena. El final ya no debe parecer perfecto. Debe mostrar cómo se fabrica una ficción cuando todo sale mal.": "The press cards fit together and reveal a note on the back: the promotional livestream never stopped. The audience has seen everything—the crooked wig, the argument over the umbrella, and your attempt to hide behind a plant that was far too small.\n\n서미라 watches the viewer count and makes a dangerously televisual decision: instead of hiding the accident, she will turn it into the scene. The ending must no longer look perfect. It must show how fiction is made when everything goes wrong.",
  "Las notas de interpretación terminan con una instrucción subrayada: «No finjas estar solo». Comprendes que la silla vacía del storyboard no esperaba al protagonista ausente; reservaba un lugar para cualquiera capaz de compartir el plano.\n\nLa directora abre el canal de comunicación con todo el estudio. Falta una última decisión, y esta vez no será una orden. Será una propuesta construida entre todos.": "The acting notes end with an underlined instruction: “Don't pretend you're alone.” You realise that the empty chair in the storyboard was not waiting for the missing lead; it reserved a place for anyone capable of sharing the shot.\n\nThe director opens the communication channel to the entire studio. One final decision remains, and this time it will not be an order. It will be a proposal built by everyone together.",
  "떠나다 = marcharse · 마지막 장면 = escena final.": "떠나다 = leave · 마지막 장면 = final scene.",
  "-다고 했어요 (G089) transmite una afirmación. Una orden sería -(으)라고, una pregunta -냐고 y una propuesta -자고.": "-다고 했어요 (G089) transmits a statement. An order would be -(으)라고, a question -냐고 and a proposal -자고.",
  "Dijo que el protagonista se marcha en la escena final.": "He said the protagonist is leaving at the final scene.",
  "Le ordenó al protagonista que se marchara en la escena final.": "He ordered the protagonist to leave at the final scene.",
  "Preguntó si el protagonista se marchaba en la escena final.": "He asked if the protagonist was leaving at the final scene.",
  "Propuso que todos se marcharan en la escena final.": "He proposed that everyone leave at the final scene.",
  "¿Qué decisión dejó escrita la guionista?": "What decision did the screenwriter leave in writing?",
  "소품 팀 = utilería · 가짜 = falso, de atrezo.": "소품 팀 = props team · 가짜 = fake, a prop.",
  "Con sustantivo + 이라고/라고 했어요 se cita una afirmación: 가짜라고 했어요 = «dijo que era falso».": "A noun + 이라고/라고 했어요 quotes a statement: 가짜라고 했어요 = “said it was fake”.",
  "Preguntó dónde estaba el paraguas azul.": "He asked where the blue umbrella was.",
  "Dijo que el paraguas azul era falso.": "He said the blue umbrella was fake.",
  "Pidió que usaran un paraguas azul falso.": "He asked for a fake blue umbrella.",
  "Propuso pintar de azul el paraguas.": "He proposed to paint the umbrella blue.",
  "¿Qué informó el equipo de utilería?": "What did the prop team report?",
  "해 질 무렵 = al caer el sol · 가장 좋다 = ser lo mejor.": "해 질 무렵 = around sunset · 가장 좋다 = be best / ideal.",
  "좋다고 했어요 es discurso indirecto declarativo (G089): conserva la afirmación, no la convierte en pregunta ni orden.": "좋다고 했어요 is declarative indirect discourse (G089): it retains the affirmation, does not make it a question or order.",
  "Ordenó apagar todas las luces al anochecer.": "He ordered all lights out by nightfall.",
  "Preguntó si quedaba luz al anochecer.": "He asked if there was any light at nightfall.",
  "Dijo que la luz del atardecer era la mejor.": "He said the sunset light was the best.",
  "Propuso rodar únicamente de noche.": "He proposed to shoot only at night.",
  "¿Qué dijo el director de iluminación?": "What did the lighting director say?",
  "대사 = diálogo · 뻔하다 = obvio, predecible.": "대사 = line / dialogue · 뻔하다 = obvious, predictable.",
  "El adjetivo se reporta con -다고 하다: 뻔하다고 했어요. La frase informa una opinión, no una instrucción.": "The adjective is reported with -다고 하다: 뻔하다고 했어요. The phrase reports an opinion, not an instruction.",
  "Dijo que era demasiado larga.": "He said it was too long.",
