  "켜다 = encender. La orden original sería «카메라를 켜!».": "켜다 = turn on. The original command would be «카메라를 켜!».",
  "Una orden citada usa V-(으)라고 하다 (G090): 켜다 termina en vocal → 켜라고 했어요.": "A command cited uses V-(으)라고 하다 (G090): 켜다 ends in vowel → 켜라고 했어요.",
  "La directora dijo que encendieran primero la cámara.": "The director said to turn on the camera first.",
  "기다리다 = esperar · 표시선 = marca de posición.": "기다리다 = wait · 표시선 = position marker.",
  "La raíz termina en vocal: 기다리다 → 기다리라고 했어요 (G090).": "The root ends in vowel: 기다리다 → 기다리라고 했어요 (G090).",
  "El ayudante dijo a los extras que esperaran detrás de la marca.": "The assistant told the extras to wait behind the brand.",
  "끄다 = apagar · 휴대 전화 = teléfono móvil.": "끄다 = turn off · 휴대 전화 = mobile phone.",
  "끄다 pierde 다 y toma -라고: 끄라고 했어요. 끈다고 reportaría una afirmación.": "끄다 loses 다 and takes -라고: 끄라고 했어요. 끈다고 would report a statement.",
  "El técnico de sonido dijo que apagaran todos los teléfonos.": "The sound technician said to turn off all the phones.",
  "가발 = peluca · 고정하다 = fijar.": "가발 = wig · 고정하다 = secure / fix.",
  "El mandato indirecto exige -(으)라고 (G090): 고정하라고 했어요.": "The indirect mandate requires -(으)라고 (G090): 고정하라고 했어요.",
  "La jefa de maquillaje dijo que fijaran la peluca antes de mojarse.": "The makeup manager said to fix the wig before getting wet.",
  "들다 = sostener · 왼손 = mano izquierda.": "들다 = hold · 왼손 = left hand.",
  "Con una raíz acabada en ㄹ, la orden citada es 들라고; 들으라고 pertenece a 듣다, escuchar.": "With a root finished in ㄹ, the command cited is 들라고; 들으라고 belongs to 듣다, listen.",
  "La responsable de continuidad dijo que sujetaran el paraguas con la mano izquierda.": "The continuance officer said to hold the umbrella with your left hand.",
  "슬프다 = estar triste · 결말 = desenlace.": "슬프다 = be sad · 결말 = ending.",
  "Pregunta indirecta con adjetivo: 슬프냐고 물었습니다 (G091). -다고 la convertiría en afirmación.": "Indirect question with adjective: 슬프냐고 물었습니다 (G091). -다고 would make it an affirmation.",
  "Construye: «La periodista preguntó si el final era triste».": "Build: “The reporter asked whether the ending was sad.”",
